    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Repo Rate is the interest rate at which RBI lends short-term money to commercial banks, whereas Reverse Repo Rate is the rate at which RBI borrows from banks.",
        "Direct Tax burden cannot be shifted (e.g., Income Tax), while Indirect Tax burden is passed to the final consumer (e.g., GST).",
        "FDI involves direct ownership of physical assets and active management, whereas FPI involves passive investment in financial securities like shares and bonds."
      ],
